ow can we best deal with big egos in  the workplace  or elsewhere well  big egos aren't the problem unhealthy  egos are the problem  i hope you have a big ego there's a big  difference between  uh being self-confident and being  conceited  being self-confident means you think  you're good  being conceited means you think you're  better than other people i hope you have  big egos our  our goal is to help people build their  confidence so that they see themselves  as good but we never want people to  think themselves as better as others  so if we are working with people who  think they are better than us  uh that's the question so number one is  uh  uh sometimes uh big egos and healthy  egos  are masquerading as uh masquerade  in place of um insecurity so  sometimes attacking them and thinking  that their egos are outsized  maybe they are just insecure and they're  compensating for something  maybe they're uncertain or unsure so  strangely enough a little empathy  matters  but if somebody truly does have an  outsized ego the way i think they're  better than everyone else  just enjoy it smile go about your job  don't worry about it  as long as they're not because taking  them on is only going to  create things and make things worse i  throughout my career i've worked with  people who like to  posture and prove and i just sort of  smile and let them have their way  kill them with kindness you know don't  let it get to me  uh because if it gets to me i become  competitive with them and i just sort of  focus on the work that i'm doing  um hopefully that helps a little bit  okay these are all over the place um so  let's try another one here emma  asks um how can we learn to be  more decisive  it's about taking a risk right making a  decision now  with anything that we're learning um you  can practice small  you don't have to start practicing being  decisive with big things  you can start practicing to being  decisive with small things  what do you want for dinner tonight s