 what do you do  if you're too far in your career to make  a pivot  but aren't feeling fulfilled ah so the  question is  are you ever too far in your career to  make a pivot  um sometimes we have golden handcuffs  that's true where we're in a position  where things are good and we don't want  to let go and throw it away  um there are ways to pivot inside our  careers  but when you say make a pivot i mean if  you're not enjoying yourself  and it's just the stability or or the or  the  um the salary that's making you uh  not want to make a change if you have a  partner talk to your partner  because it's going to be something that  you can you have to make that decision  together  if you don't have a partner that you  that you're you're with um talk to your  friends and family  you will find that you will have more  courage to make a difficult decision  like this  if you have at least one person who  believes in you and loves you and says  you got this even if it doesn't work out  i'll still be  there with you we'll figure this out  together how can we do this in a way  that um we can make you happy uh try  try talking with somebody about it if  you aren't feeling fulfilled  and by the way if you're not feeling  fulfilled it's not necessarily you have  to abandon your career sometimes you can  find a new job within the company you're  in  you talk to if you have a good  relationship with your leader sit down  and say i think i'm curious about other  things  um uh and start poking around outside so  yeah  your happiness is way more important uh  what else we got here  uh charlene asks how do i manage the  expectations of others  not setting them too high or too low  ah i struggle with this i try and say  yes to everybody  and what i've learned is saying no has  been one of the most valuable skills  i've learned i'm still not great at it  because what i learned is when i try and  say yes to everybody i end up  disappointing multiple  people and so learning to say no  saying you know and saying ah i so want  to do that  unfortunately my schedule this week is  insane  and i just can't get to it this week um  you know the old adage is also um keep  expectations low and then over deliver  um that's also really fun to do um  obviously  uh it's fun to set high expectations but  if you want to manage expectations  either be realistic or or or under  promise here's one little trick that i  learned  somebody said when can you have that  done by and the mistake i used to make i  used to say  tuesday now i say next week  right and then hopefully i'll get them  to tuesday and they're really excited  but if i get it to them on friday  it's fine um what time do you want to  meet uh  three o'clock or this afternoon  and that way i can better manage my work  if i'm  bad at managing my workload or things  are taking longer than i expect  i leave the a little broader uh  boundaries on  the sandbox that has helped me a great  deal i hope that helps you too  charlene okay last question from anna  uh how can we balance and lost my  balance that was really funny i actually  lost my balance  when i read the word balance okay how  can we balance  full-time work with creative projects  creatively uh so um separation of church  and state i'm a great believer in it  um work is for work and home is for home  um and sometimes they blend sometimes we  have to bring work home  um but i'm a great believer what's  helped me believe it or not is  scheduling time  so i'll actually schedule time for  creative exercises  um so in my schedule it'll i'll have a  block off  that's for me to do creative things and  that way when i'm building my schedule  or when things are coming in somebody  says can you meet at four o'clock on  thursday i say  sorry i have something else then what i  have then  is to do something creative to do a  creative exercise  so i found that to be really helpful um  also that way i'm not left to the end of  the day to do my creative things every 